{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-11T22:33:42.562Z","data":{"text":"Done. Both verifies green; all six files are inside the task's scope plus the result file.\n\n**Summary of work for task 1 of change 178:**\n\n- **`src/core/foundation/gitattributes-block.ts`** (new): exports the two markers, `GITATTRIBUTES_BLOCK` (`# OSQ:GITATTRIBUTES:START\\n* text=auto\\n# OSQ:GITATTRIBUTES:END`), and `writeGitattributesBlock(projectRoot)` modeled on `rules-block.ts` — writes `B\\n` for missing/empty files, prepends `B\\n\\n` when no block exists, replaces a differing block in place byte-for-byte, leaves a current block untouched, returns true only on a write. Tagged `@scenario` ×2 and `@adr 003`.\n- **`src/core/foundation/init.ts`**: `InitResult` gained `updatedGitattributes`; extracted the managed-block writes into a private `writeManagedBlocks` helper so `scaffoldProject` stays at 70 lines (under the 80-line budget).\n- **`src/cli/init.ts`**: prints `  updated  .gitattributes (line endings)\\n` after the project-rules line, tagged for both scenarios.\n- **`.gitattributes`**: managed block + blank line at the top, the four existing lines unchanged below.\n- **`README.md`**: added the `.gitattributes` line after `.env.example *` in `## What it puts in your repo`.\n- **`tests/init-gitattributes.test.ts`** (new): proves every table row of both scenarios through `initCommand` in temp dirs via the `stdout` writer, plus that this repo's `.gitattributes` starts with the block and README holds the new line."}}
